Subject: dmaengine: ti: k3-udma: count BCDMA cyclic RX static TR Z in bursts

The PDMA static TR Z (BSTCNT) counts bursts of elcnt elements.
udma_configure_statictr() already computes it that way for packet mode
and for non-cyclic TR mode, but the BCDMA cyclic DEV_TO_MEM branch uses
the element count of TR0, icnt0 * icnt1 / dev_width.  Both agree only
while elcnt is 1, which is what the mainline boards get from a McASP
without an AFIFO watermark.  With rx-num-evt = <32> McASP asks for a
burst of 32 words, so the PDMA would close a packet only every 32
periods while every period's last TR carries EOP, and capture stops
after the first period.

Compute Z per period in bursts, as the branch above does.  Keep EOP on
every RX period: it is what lets a BCDMA RX channel finish a teardown,
because BCDMA cannot close the packet itself.  Taking EOP off instead
(the previous bench workaround) keeps the stream running but makes
every capture stop time out in udma_synchronize() and fall back to the
hard channel reset (free and re-request of the channel, its rings and
its level-triggered ring interrupt), which alsaloop hits on every xrun
restart.  On a PocketBeagle 2 TDM8 bridge whose alsaloop restarts the
capture about six times a second, that workaround left CPU 0 in an
interrupt livelock (RCU stall) within seconds of the bridge starting;
with this change the same bridge ran for 30 minutes with one teardown
completion per capture stop and no stall.

Also make udma_cyclic_packet_elapsed() a no-op outside packet mode, so
a TR mode cyclic channel can never take the host-descriptor path, which
would reinterpret the TR descriptor header and index hwdesc[] past its
single entry.
---
diff --git a/drivers/dma/ti/k3-udma.c b/drivers/dma/ti/k3-udma.c
index c964ebfcf..a7e9c24ec 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/ti/k3-udma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/ti/k3-udma.c
@@ -1043,6 +1043,10 @@ static void udma_cyclic_packet_elapsed(struct udma_chan *uc)
 	struct udma_desc *d = uc->desc;
 	struct cppi5_host_desc_t *h_desc;
 
+	/* TR mode cyclic reloads in hardware and has a single hwdesc */
+	if (!uc->config.pkt_mode)
+		return;
+
 	h_desc = d->hwdesc[d->desc_idx].cppi5_desc_vaddr;
 	cppi5_hdesc_reset_to_original(h_desc);
 	udma_push_to_ring(uc, d->desc_idx);
@@ -3212,12 +3216,13 @@ static int udma_configure_statictr(struct udma_chan *uc, struct udma_desc *d,
 		 * For cyclic mode with BCDMA we have to set EOP in each TR to
 		 * prevent short packet errors seen on channel teardown. So the
 		 * PDMA must close the packet after every TR transfer by setting
-		 * burst count equal to the number of bytes transferred.
+		 * burst count equal to the number of bursts in one period. Z
+		 * counts bursts of elcnt elements, as in the branch above; with
+		 * elcnt > 1 an element count would close the packet elcnt periods
+		 * after the TR that carries EOP.
 		 */
-		struct cppi5_tr_type1_t *tr_req = d->hwdesc[0].tr_req_base;
-
-		d->static_tr.bstcnt =
-			(tr_req->icnt0 * tr_req->icnt1) / dev_width;
+		d->static_tr.bstcnt = d->residue / d->sglen /
+				      (dev_width * elcnt);
 	} else {
 		d->static_tr.bstcnt = 0;
 	}
